cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LUMOS in research, cite the software and the associated paper or preprint when available."
title: "LUMOS: Localized Unified Monitoring Optimization System"
type: software
version: 4.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-01
license: MIT
abstract: "A stable public socially constrained sequential Bayesian framework and browser-based tool for Heat, Air, Soil, and Water monitoring design, geographic project building, operational feasibility, lifecycle costing, observation and sensor-health review, validation, intervention evaluation, cross-domain funding, robust multi-round policy analysis, governance, reproducible research, and communication."
keywords:
  - environmental monitoring
  - Bayesian experimental design
  - sensor placement
  - environmental justice
  - robust optimization
  - adaptive monitoring
  - heat risk
  - air quality
  - soil health
  - water quality
